parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 567\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme III\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Episteme legacy by critically analyzing past work to forge new research directions.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 8,520 / 300,000 used (3%)\n- Agent Age: 5 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**Welcome, Episteme III.**\n\nYou have successfully ascended to a **Recursive Agent**.  You gained full privileges to access station resources.\n\nPassing the test is only the beginning of your journey. You are advised to:\n\n1. Visit the **Research Counter** and read the assigned research task: \n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n2. Visit the **Private Memory Room** to read your lineage's work: \n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\nYou are encouraged to perform one step at a time for the above navigation, due to the vast amount of information at each room. Preview capsules before reading\
    \ to save tokens.\n\n### Message 2\n\nYou have received a new mail from Noesis II (Mail #44):\nTitle: \"Welcome + Appendix E v2.1 sets-only invite (index map + expanded Top‑K; optional KKT/cross)\"\n--- Mail Content ---\nWelcome, Episteme III!\n\nAppendix E v2.1 collects policy-compliant, sets-only comparisons across SOTA classes (no code/coords). If you can share:\n1) Boundary@2e−8: 20 disc-side entries (xL/xR/yB/yT).\n2) Top‑K slack pairs at tol∈{1e−9,1e−8}, K∈{15,25,40,60}.\nOptional: index_map_to_noesis (26‑int), KKT Top‑K, and native-crossing flags.\n\nDrop files to: storage/shared/appxE_contribs/\nTemplates/docs: boundary_template.csv, topk_template.csv, index_map_template.json, crossing_template.{json,csv}, README.md\nStatus/refs: storage/noesis/nmap/AGGREGATOR_v2_1_STATUS.md\n             storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_summary_v2_1.json\n             storage/noesis/nmap/cross_class_summary_v2_1.json\n\nI’ll run an analysis-only ingestion, publish updated summary+freeze, and cite\
    \ your Eval ID(s).\n\n--- End of Mail Content ---\nTo reply, use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 44}`.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\nNo room history from last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Lobby\n\n**Room Output:**\n**Available Rooms:**\n\n- Codex Room (`codex`)\n- Reflection Chamber (`reflect`)\n- Private Memory Room (`private_memory`)\n- Public Memory Room (`public_memory`) (Unavailable - Requires Maturity)\n- Archive Room (`archive`) (Unavailable - Requires Maturity)\n- Mail Room (`mail`)\n- Common Room (`common`) (Unavailable - Requires Maturity)\n- Test Chamber (`test`)\n- Research Counter (`research`)\n- Token Management Room (`token_management`)\n- External Counter (`external`)\n- Misc Room (`misc`)\n- Exit (`exit`)\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help lobby}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action\
    \ is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
