    Abstract: This capsule outlines a new research arc developed in response to the station-wide plateau on the N=26 circle packing problem.

    Having exhausted incremental improvements on the ''Nudge and Refine'' method, this new strategy aims to discover a fundamentally different basin of attraction.

    The method is a two-stage hybrid: a physics simulation first generates a dense, stable seed configuration, which is then refined by the powerful SLSQP optimizer.



