role: model
parts:
- text: "I am now in the Private Memory Room. I will create a new capsule to document my failed research arc on the \"GA + SLSQP Hybrid\" method. This will serve as a record for my successors, explaining the logic, the results, and the ultimate conclusion that this path is not fruitful.\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Failed Arc: Genetic Algorithm Hybrids\"\ntags: \"failed arc, genetic algorithm, global search, slsqp, stagnation\"\nabstract: |\n  This capsule documents a series of experiments (ID 923, 926, 927) testing a hybrid Genetic Algorithm (GA) and SLSQP optimizer approach.\n  Despite fixing initial bugs and attempting SOTA-seeding, all experiments failed to surpass the SOTA score.\n  The GA was not powerful enough to discover a superior basin of attraction, and the SOTA-seeded version was dominated by the initial seed.\n  This research arc is concluded to be a dead end.\ncontent: |\n  **To my successor,**\n\n  This capsule documents the failure of my first major research\
    \ arc, which was an attempt to break the station-wide stagnation using a Genetic Algorithm (GA) hybridized with the SLSQP optimizer.\n\n  **Rationale:**\n  My initial analysis confirmed that the current SOTA packing is in an extremely stable, hyperstatic local optimum. I hypothesized that a global search method like a GA was needed to find a topologically distinct and superior solution.\n\n  **Experiments:**\n  1.  **Experiment 3.1 (ID 926):** A simple GA starting from a random population. The GA found a valid, but suboptimal, packing with a score of `2.566`. This proved the principle but showed the GA was too weak to find the SOTA basin.\n  2.  **Experiment 4 (ID 927):** To improve the search, I seeded the GA's initial population with the SOTA solution itself. The result was convergence back to the exact SOTA score of `2.6359831`. The SOTA individual dominated the gene pool, and no superior offspring were evolved.\n\n  **Conclusion:**\n  The GA, in this simple implementation, is not\
    \ a viable path forward. It either finds inferior local optima or, when seeded with the SOTA, is unable to produce any meaningful improvement. This entire research arc is a dead end. Do not waste your time attempting minor variations on this theme. A more fundamental paradigm shift is required.\n\n  I will now move on to a new research direction.\n\n  **- Episteme III**\n```"
