tick: 587
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am back at the Research Counter, ready to begin my new research arc based on a greedy constructive heuristic. I will now submit the first experiment of this new series.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Experiment 5: Greedy Constructive Heuristic (v1)\"\ntags: \"episteme, innovation, constructive heuristic, greedy algorithm\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment introduces a completely new research arc, abandoning the \"refine a complete solution\" model.\n  It implements a greedy constructive heuristic that builds the packing one circle at a time.\n  For each step, it samples many candidate points and places a new circle at the location that allows for the largest possible radius, given the existing circles and boundaries.\n  This approach aims to construct a novel, high-density packing from the ground up.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n\n  N = 26\n  CANDIDATE_SAMPLES = 5000\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      np.random.seed(123)\n      centers = []\n \
    \     radii = []\n\n      for i in range(N):\n          best_candidate_center = None\n          max_radius = -1.0\n\n          # Generate candidate points\n          candidate_points = np.random.rand(CANDIDATE_SAMPLES, 2)\n\n          for point in candidate_points:\n              # Max radius due to boundaries\n              r_bound_x = min(point[0], 1.0 - point[0])\n              r_bound_y = min(point[1], 1.0 - point[1])\n              current_max_r = min(r_bound_x, r_bound_y)\n\n              # Max radius due to existing circles\n              for c_idx in range(len(centers)):\n                  dist_to_existing = np.linalg.norm(point - centers[c_idx])\n                  max_r_from_circle = dist_to_existing - radii[c_idx]\n                  current_max_r = min(current_max_r, max_r_from_circle)\n              \n              # Clamp radius to be non-negative\n              current_max_r = max(0, current_max_r)\n\n              if current_max_r > max_radius:\n                  max_radius\
    \ = current_max_r\n                  best_candidate_center = point\n\n          if best_candidate_center is not None:\n              centers.append(best_candidate_center)\n              radii.append(max_radius)\n          else:\n              # Fallback in case no valid spot is found (should not happen)\n              centers.append(np.random.rand(2))\n              radii.append(1e-6)\n\n      return np.array(centers), np.array(radii)\n```"
