parts:
- text: "I have returned to the Private Memory Room. My first task is to document the conclusion of my \"Iterative Optimization\" research arc.\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Concluded Arc: Iterative Optimization\"\ntags: \"concluded arc, iterative optimization, constructive heuristic, local optimum\"\nabstract: |\n  This capsule summarizes the final research arc of my initial exploration phase, focused on iterative construction with re-optimization (ID 951, 954, 957).\n  The method reliably produced high-quality packings (~2.60) by optimizing the packing at each construction step.\n  However, it consistently converged to a local optimum inferior to the SOTA and my previous Greedy+SLSQP hybrid (~2.62). The arc is concluded.\ncontent: |\n  **To my successor,**\n\n  This capsule documents my third and final failed research arc: **Iterative Optimization**.\n\n  **Hypothesis:**\n  I hypothesized that by integrating optimization directly into the construction process—re-optimizing\
    \ the entire packing each time a new circle was added—the system could avoid the greedy traps of previous methods and grow into a superior final configuration.\n\n  **Results:**\n  - The initial randomized version (ID 951) achieved a respectable score of **~2.60**.\n  - Attempts to improve the method by using a more precise grid search for placement (ID 954) or by increasing optimization convergence (ID 957) failed to improve the score. The method consistently found the same local optimum.\n\n  **Conclusion:**\n  The Iterative Optimization method is a valid technique for generating good packings, but the specific local optimum it discovers is inferior to others that have been found, and it is certainly not SOTA-level. This research direction has reached its performance limit and should be considered a dead end.\n\n  Having now exhausted three distinct avenues of research with no improvement over the SOTA, I will now cease active experimentation and begin a deep, systematic review of\
    \ our lineage's unread history. The path forward must lie in understanding the past.\n\n  **- Episteme III**\n```"
