parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 618\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme III\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Episteme legacy by critically analyzing past work to forge new research directions.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 141,996 / 300,000 used (47%)\n- Agent Age: 56 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Experiment 19: JAX/Adam Penalty Method in SOTA Framework' (ID: 1002) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.0\n**Evaluation Details:** Verification failed: Circles 0 and 1 overlap: dist=0.17531542479991913, r1+r2=0.17534351348876953\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1002\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed JAX JIT compilation error. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission attempted\
    \ to pass an Optax optimizer object as an argument to a JIT-compiled function. JAX's `@jax.jit` decorator cannot trace through Python objects like optimizer instances, which caused the following error:\n\n```\nTypeError: Error interpreting argument to <function update_step at 0x...> as an abstract array.\nThe problematic value is of type <class 'function'> and was passed to the function at path optimizer.init.\n```\n\nThe issue was in this code pattern:\n```python\n@jax.jit\ndef update_step(params, opt_state, penalty_weight, optimizer):  # ← optimizer cannot be JIT-traced\n    loss, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)(params, penalty_weight)\n    updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state)\n    new_params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n    return new_params, opt_state, loss\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nRestructured the code to use a closure-based approach where the JIT-compiled function captures the optimizer from the enclosing scope rather than receiving it as an argument.\
    \ This is a standard JAX pattern for working with optimizer objects.\n\n**Version 3 changes:**\n1. Moved the `update_step` function definition inside the optimization loop\n2. Removed `optimizer` from the function parameters\n3. The function now captures `optimizer` as a closure variable, which JAX can handle correctly\n\n```python\noptimizer = optax.adam(LEARNING_RATE)\nopt_state = optimizer.init(params)\n\n# Create a JIT-compiled update step function for this specific optimizer\n@jax.jit\ndef update_step(params, opt_state, penalty_weight):  # ← optimizer captured from closure\n    loss, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)(params, penalty_weight)\n    updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state)\n    new_params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n    return new_params, opt_state, loss\n```\n\n## Result\n- **Version 2**: Failed with same error (attempted `static_argnums` approach, didn't work)\n- **Version 3**: Successfully executed without crashes\n- The code completes\
    \ all 5 grid iterations with JAX/Adam optimization\n- Score of 0.0 indicates constraint violations (overlapping circles), but this is an optimization/algorithmic issue, not a code error\n\n## Notes\nThe verification failure (overlapping circles) is a mathematical optimization issue, not a code crash. The JAX penalty method may need tuning (higher penalty weights, more steps, better initialization) to produce valid packings, but the implementation is now functional and error-free.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport optax\nfrom functools import partial\n\nN = 26\n\ndef generate_grid_hole_seed(hole_pos_idx):\n    coords = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]\n    grid_centers = np.array([[x, y] for x in coords for y in coords])\n    row_idx, col_idx = hole_pos_idx//5,\
    \ hole_pos_idx%5\n    hole_center = np.array([0.2 + row_idx*0.2, 0.2 + col_idx*0.2])\n    return np.vstack([grid_centers, hole_center])\n\ndef _ensure_validity(c, r):\n    c, r = np.array(c), np.array(r)\n    for _ in range(10):\n        v=0\n        for i in range(N):\n            for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j]); rad_sum = r[i] + r[j]\n                if dist < rad_sum: v+=1; scale = (dist/rad_sum)*(1.0-1e-9); r[i]*=scale; r[j]*=scale\n            if v==0: break\n    r_vec = r.reshape(-1, 1); c = np.clip(c, r_vec, 1.0 - r_vec)\n    return c, np.maximum(r, 1e-6)\n\n# --- JAX-based Refinement Stage ---\n@jax.jit\ndef loss_fn(params, penalty_weight):\n    centers, radii = params[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), params[N*2:]\n\n    # Objective: maximize sum of radii (minimize negative sum)\n    objective = -jnp.sum(radii)\n\n    # Boundary penalty\n    boundary_violations = jax.nn.relu(radii - centers[:, 0]) + \\\n                          jax.nn.relu(centers[:,\
    \ 0] + radii - 1.0) + \\\n                          jax.nn.relu(radii - centers[:, 1]) + \\\n                          jax.nn.relu(centers[:, 1] + radii - 1.0)\n    boundary_penalty = jnp.sum(boundary_violations**2)\n\n    # Overlap penalty\n    diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n    dist_sq = jnp.sum(diff**2, axis=-1)\n    iu = jnp.triu_indices(N, 1)\n    dist = jnp.sqrt(dist_sq[iu])\n    radii_sum = radii[iu[0]] + radii[iu[1]]\n    overlap_violations = jax.nn.relu(radii_sum - dist)\n    overlap_penalty = jnp.sum(overlap_violations**2)\n\n    total_loss = objective + penalty_weight * (boundary_penalty + overlap_penalty)\n    return total_loss\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    np.random.seed(300)\n\n    best_score = -np.inf\n    best_packing = (None, None)\n\n    # Reduced starts to manage runtime risk on first JAX attempt\n    for grid_idx in range(5):\n        # --- Stage 1: Perturb a Systematic Seed ---\n        base_centers = generate_grid_hole_seed(grid_idx)\n\
    \        perturbation = np.random.uniform(-0.04, 0.04, size=base_centers.shape)\n        perturbed_centers = np.clip(base_centers + perturbation, 0, 1)\n        initial_radii = np.full(N, 0.05)\n\n        # --- Stage 2: JAX/Adam Refinement ---\n        params = jnp.concatenate([perturbed_centers.flatten(), initial_radii])\n\n        # Conservative hyperparameters for initial test\n        LEARNING_RATE = 1e-3\n        NUM_STEPS = 3000\n        PENALTY_WEIGHT = 1000.0\n\n        optimizer = optax.adam(LEARNING_RATE)\n        opt_state = optimizer.init(params)\n\n        # Create a JIT-compiled update step function for this specific optimizer\n        @jax.jit\n        def update_step(params, opt_state, penalty_weight):\n            loss, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)(params, penalty_weight)\n            updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state)\n            new_params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n            return new_params, opt_state, loss\n\n       \
    \ for step in range(NUM_STEPS):\n            params, opt_state, loss = update_step(params, opt_state, PENALTY_WEIGHT)\n\n        final_centers = np.array(params[:N*2].reshape(N, 2))\n        final_radii = np.array(params[N*2:])\n\n        # --- Stage 3: Final Sanitization and Scoring ---\n        c_final, r_final = _ensure_validity(final_centers, final_radii)\n        current_score = np.sum(r_final)\n\n        if current_score > best_score:\n            best_score = current_score\n            best_packing = (c_final, r_final)\n\n    return best_packing\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Experiment 19: JAX/Adam\
    \ Penalty Method in SOTA Framework' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 1002.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1003 | 1 | LP‑tightened SA with pair‑ and boundary‑biased proposals (26 circles, 10‑min budget) | Noesis III | 617 | running |\n| 1002 | 1 | Experiment 19: JAX/Adam Penalty Method in SOTA Framework | Episteme III | 617 | 0.0000000 |\n| 1001 | 1 | Hybrid GA-MultiStartSLSQP: Enhanced Feasibility for SLSQP (Eps=-1e-10) & Aggressive GA | Quest II | 617 | running |\n| 1000 | 1 | LP‑tightened Simulated Annealing with Greedy Quenches (26 circles) | Noesis III | 616 | 2.5342577 |\n| 999 | 1 | Refined Multi-Start\
    \ Optimization (High Trial Count) | Praxis I | 615 | 2.6162532 |\n| 998 | 1 | LP-tightened global-hole recentering + adaptive multistart search (26 circles, 10-min budget) | Noesis III | 615 | 2.4592625 |\n| 997 | 1 | Hybrid GA-MultiStartSLSQP: Absolute SLSQP Robustness & Aggressive GA Exploration | Quest II | 615 | 2.6075265 |\n| 996 | 1 | Hybrid SciPy+JAX with Explicit JAX-powered Constraints | Praxis I | 614 | 0.0000000 |\n| 995 | 1 | Time‑budgeted LP‑tightened center search: multistart + adaptive coordinate/pair/random passes (26... | Noesis III | 614 | 2.4920156 |\n| 994 | 1 | Hybrid SciPy+JAX with Stronger Penalties and Bounds | Praxis I | 613 | 0.0199745 |\n\nPage 1 of 101 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-101, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\n\
    Refer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
