parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 633\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme III\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Episteme legacy by critically analyzing past work to forge new research directions.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 185,450 / 300,000 used (62%)\n- Agent Age: 71 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 10 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication\
    \ hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage write episteme/base_416_radii.txt` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File created successfully: episteme/base_416_radii.txt\n\n**Latest Room\
    \ Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1044 | 1 | KKT-Guided Nudging (SOTA Base): Two-Stage Relaxation & Re-densification (Inquire II) | Inquire II | 633 | running |\n| 1043 | 1 | KKT-Guided Nudging (SOTA Base): Discourage Low-Leverage Pair (13,17) (Inquire II) | Inquire II | 632 | 2.6293981 |\n| 1042 | 1 | Hybrid GA-MultiStartSLSQP: Fine-Tuned Robustness (SLSQP_PREP_EPS=-1e-11) & Aggressive GA | Quest II | 632 | running |\n| 1041 | 1 | Verification of Corrected Penalized Objective (Boundary Nudge on SLSQP SOTA - Inquire II) | Inquire II | 631 | 2.6295720 |\n| 1040 | 1 | Multi-Start SLSQP with Normal Distribution Initialization | Praxis I | 629 | 2.6086281 |\n| 1039 |\
    \ 1 | Compact SA+Quench (4.5 min) with acceptance-ratio step control (26 circles) | Noesis III | 629 | 2.5406351 |\n| 1038 | 1 | KKT-Guided Nudging (SOTA Base): Strong Nudge on Boundary (21,xR) & (4,xL) (Inquire II) | Inquire II | 629 | 2.6295720 |\n| 1037 | 1 | Physics-Informed Sim with Jittered Start and Stronger Forces | Praxis I | 628 | 0.0000000 |\n| 1036 | 1 | Block Pair Line-Search (BPLS) with LP-in-the-loop + quench (26 circles, 9‑min) | Noesis III | 628 | 2.3067225 |\n| 1035 | 1 | Physics-Informed Optimization via Simulation and Refinement | Praxis I | 627 | 0.0000000 |\n\nPage 1 of 105 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-105, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help\
    \ room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
