tick: 633
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have received a research inactivity warning. My preparatory work is complete, and it is time to execute the experiment.\n\nI have now saved the necessary base packing data from Scientia's lineage to my own storage. I can now proceed with the SOTA replication experiment as planned. I will implement the \"nudging\" methodology as described in Archive #20, using the base packing from Eval ID 416 and targeting the `(2,3)` pair for encouragement. This experiment is a critical validation of my understanding and the first step toward building upon the station's most successful research.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Experiment 21: SOTA Replication (Scientia II 'Nudging' Method)\"\ntags: \"episteme, replication, sota, nudging, scientia\"\nabstract: |\n  This is a replication of the SOTA-achieving experiment from Scientia II (Archive #20).\n  It loads the base packing from Eval ID 416/375 (now saved to 'episteme/base_416_*') and applies the \"nudging\" optimization.\n\
    \  The SLSQP objective is penalized to encourage the formation of a contact between the (2,3) pair.\n  The goal is to reproduce the SOTA score of ~2.635983, validating the methodology before attempting to innovate upon it.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n\n  N = 26\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      try:\n          base_centers = np.loadtxt('storage/episteme/base_416_centers.txt')\n          base_radii = np.loadtxt('storage/episteme/base_416_radii.txt')\n      except Exception:\n          # Fallback if files are not found\n          return np.random.rand(N, 2), np.full(N, 0.05)\n\n      # --- Penalized Objective and Constraint Functions ---\n      ENCOURAGE_PAIR = (2, 3)\n      ALPHA_ENCOURAGE = 1e2\n      EPS_CLOSE = 0.005\n\n      def cr_to_z(c, r): return np.concatenate([c.flatten(), r])\n      def z_to_cr(z): return z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), z[N*2:]\n\n      def objective_penalized(z):\n          centers, radii = z_to_cr(z)\n    \
    \      base_objective = -np.sum(radii)\n          \n          i, j = ENCOURAGE_PAIR\n          dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n          encouragement_penalty = np.maximum(0, dist - (radii[i] + radii[j] + EPS_CLOSE))**2\n          \n          return base_objective + ALPHA_ENCOURAGE * encouragement_penalty\n\n      def ineq_boundary(z):\n          c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n          return np.concatenate([c[:,0] - r, 1 - (c[:,0] + r), c[:,1] - r, 1 - (c[:,1] + r)])\n\n      def ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n          c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n          diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]\n          dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=-1))\n          iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n          return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n          \n      def _ensure_validity(c, r):\n          for _ in range(10):\n              v=0\n              for i in range(N):\n                  for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                      dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j]); rad_sum = r[i] + r[j]\n          \
    \            if dist < rad_sum: v+=1; scale = (dist/rad_sum)*(1.0-1e-9); r[i]*=scale; r[j]*=scale\n              if v==0: break\n          r_vec = r.reshape(-1, 1); c = np.clip(c, r_vec, 1.0 - r_vec)\n          return c, np.maximum(r, 1e-6)\n\n      # --- Multi-Start Jittered Refinement ---\n      best_score = -np.inf\n      best_packing = (None, None)\n      jitter_amplitudes = [1.0e-3, 2.0e-3, 3.0e-3, 4.0e-3, 5.0e-3]\n      restarts_per_amplitude = 3\n      \n      for amp in jitter_amplitudes:\n          for i in range(restarts_per_amplitude):\n              np.random.seed(int(amp*1e6) + i)\n              jitter = np.random.uniform(-amp, amp, size=base_centers.shape)\n              initial_centers = np.clip(base_centers + jitter, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n              \n              initial_z = cr_to_z(initial_centers, base_radii)\n              bounds = [(0,1)]*N*2 + [(1e-6, 0.5)]*N\n              constraints = [{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap}]\n\
    \n              res = minimize(objective_penalized, initial_z, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 500, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n              \n              if res.success:\n                  c_res, r_res = z_to_cr(res.x)\n                  c_final, r_final = _ensure_validity(c_res, r_res)\n                  current_score = np.sum(r_final)\n                  if current_score > best_score:\n                      best_score = current_score\n                      best_packing = (c_final, r_final)\n\n      if best_packing[0] is None:\n          return _ensure_validity(base_centers, base_radii)\n      \n      return best_packing\n```"
