tick: 637
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully identified the top 5 near-contact pairs. The slack values are incredibly small, essentially at the limit of floating-point precision. This confirms the hyperstatic nature of the SOTA packing and provides a clear set of targets for my systematic nudging experiment.\n\nI will now implement the experiment. I will create a script that runs the \"nudging\" optimization for each of these 5 pairs, one after the other, within a single execution. The script will keep track of the best score found across all 5 nudging runs and return the corresponding packing. This is the \"shotgun\" approach I planned, directly following the \"Future Work\" suggestion from Archive #20.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Experiment 22: Systematic Nudging of Top 5 Near-Contacts\"\ntags: \"episteme, sota attempt, nudging, systematic exploration\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment implements the 'Systematic Nudging' strategy, building on my failure to replicate the SOTA. Instead\
    \ of targeting a single pair, this script iterates through the top 5 near-contact pairs identified in Analysis 2.\n  For each of the 5 pairs, it runs the full \"nudging\" optimization process with a penalized objective.\n  The script returns the best packing found across all 5 independent nudging attempts. This systematic exploration aims to discover a SOTA-beating structural basin.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n\n  N = 26\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      try:\n          base_centers = np.loadtxt('storage/episteme/base_416_centers.txt')\n          base_radii = np.loadtxt('storage/episteme/base_416_radii.txt')\n      except Exception:\n          return np.random.rand(N, 2), np.full(N, 0.05)\n\n      NUDGE_TARGETS = [(12, 13), (11, 12), (8, 13), (18, 25), (13, 18)]\n      \n      ALPHA_ENCOURAGE = 1e2\n      EPS_CLOSE = 0.005\n\n      def cr_to_z(c, r): return np.concatenate([c.flatten(), r])\n      def z_to_cr(z): return z[:N*2].reshape(N,\
    \ 2), z[N*2:]\n      \n      def create_penalized_objective(encourage_pair):\n          def objective_penalized(z):\n              centers, radii = z_to_cr(z)\n              base_objective = -np.sum(radii)\n              i, j = encourage_pair\n              dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n              penalty = np.maximum(0, dist - (radii[i] + radii[j] + EPS_CLOSE))**2\n              return base_objective + ALPHA_ENCOURAGE * penalty\n          return objective_penalized\n\n      def ineq_boundary(z):\n          c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n          return np.concatenate([c[:,0] - r, 1 - (c[:,0] + r), c[:,1] - r, 1 - (c[:,1] + r)])\n\n      def ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n          c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n          diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]; dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=-1))\n          iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n          return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n          \n      def _ensure_validity(c, r):\n          for _ in range(10):\n              v=0\n           \
    \   for i in range(N):\n                  for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                      dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j]); rad_sum = r[i] + r[j]\n                      if dist < rad_sum: v+=1; scale = (dist/rad_sum)*(1.0-1e-9); r[i]*=scale; r[j]*=scale\n              if v==0: break\n          r_vec = r.reshape(-1, 1); c = np.clip(c, r_vec, 1.0 - r_vec)\n          return c, np.maximum(r, 1e-6)\n\n      overall_best_score = -np.inf\n      overall_best_packing = (None, None)\n\n      for target_pair in NUDGE_TARGETS:\n          \n          objective_fn = create_penalized_objective(target_pair)\n          \n          # Run a smaller multi-start jitter for each target to manage time\n          best_score_for_target = -np.inf\n          best_packing_for_target = (None, None)\n          jitter_amplitudes = [1.0e-3, 3.0e-3, 5.0e-3]\n          restarts_per_amplitude = 2\n          \n          for amp in jitter_amplitudes:\n              for i in range(restarts_per_amplitude):\n          \
    \        np.random.seed(int(amp*1e6) + i + sum(target_pair))\n                  jitter = np.random.uniform(-amp, amp, size=base_centers.shape)\n                  initial_centers = np.clip(base_centers + jitter, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n                  \n                  initial_z = cr_to_z(initial_centers, base_radii)\n                  bounds = [(0,1)]*N*2 + [(1e-6, 0.5)]*N\n                  constraints = [{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap}]\n\n                  res = minimize(objective_fn, initial_z, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 500, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n                  \n                  if res.success:\n                      c_res, r_res = z_to_cr(res.x)\n                      c_final, r_final = _ensure_validity(c_res, r_res)\n                      current_score = np.sum(r_final)\n                      if current_score > best_score_for_target:\n                          best_score_for_target =\
    \ current_score\n                          best_packing_for_target = (c_final, r_final)\n\n          if best_score_for_target > overall_best_score:\n              overall_best_score = best_score_for_target\n              overall_best_packing = best_packing_for_target\n\n      if overall_best_packing[0] is None:\n          return _ensure_validity(base_centers, base_radii)\n      \n      return overall_best_packing\n```"
