tick: 638
role: model
parts:
- text: "My systematic nudging experiment has failed. Despite targeting the top 5 most promising near-contact pairs, every single run converged back to the base SOTA score of `2.635977`.\n\n**Conclusion of the \"Nudging\" Arc:**\nThis is a definitive and disappointing result. It not only shows that my implementation is flawed, but it also provides strong evidence that the conclusion from Quest II's paper (Archive #26) is correct: the SOTA packing is incredibly robust, and simple nudging of near-contacts is not sufficient to escape its basin of attraction. I have now spent a significant amount of time and tokens attempting to replicate and generalize a method that appears to be a dead end.\n\nI have exhausted all the \"obvious\" paths suggested by the station's history: refining the SOTA, developing new heuristics, and now, replicating the breakthrough \"nudging\" method. All have failed.\n\n**A Final, Desperate Hypothesis:**\nThere is one last variable I have not systematically explored:\
    \ the initial seed. The entire station's SOTA is built upon perturbations of the \"grid-hole\" seed. My own \"Scaled Voronoi Seeding\" method (ID 981, score `2.6302`) produced a very high-quality packing from a different set of perturbed grid-hole seeds.\n\nWhat if the base packing for the successful nudging was not the one from Eval ID 416, but a different one? The only other high-scoring base I have is the one my own method produced.\n\nMy final experiment will be a synthesis of my best method with Scientia II's.\n1.  **Generate my best seed:** I will run my \"Scaled Voronoi Seeding\" algorithm to produce a high-quality packing (`~2.63`).\n2.  **Apply nudging to *my* seed:** I will then apply the systematic nudging of the top 5 near-contacts *to my own generated packing*.\n\nThis tests a desperate but logical hypothesis: perhaps the \"nudging\" technique is only effective on a packing that is *not* the SOTA, one that has more room for structural improvement.\n\n/execute_action{submit\
    \ 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Experiment 23: Nudging My Own Voronoi-Seeded Packing\"\ntags: \"episteme, sota attempt, nudging, voronoi, synthesis\"\nabstract: |\n  After failing to improve the SOTA by nudging it, this final experiment tests a new hypothesis: perhaps nudging is only effective on a high-quality, non-SOTA packing.\n  Stage 1: My \"Scaled Voronoi Seeding\" method is used to generate my best-known packing (~2.63).\n  Stage 2: The script identifies the top 5 near-contacts in *this new packing* and applies the systematic nudging optimization to them.\n  This is a final attempt to synthesize the station's methods with my own innovations.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n\n  N = 26\n\n  def generate_grid_hole_seed(hole_pos_idx):\n      coords = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]; grid_centers = np.array([[x, y] for x in coords for y in coords])\n      row_idx, col_idx = hole_pos_idx//5, hole_pos_idx%5; hole_center = np.array([0.2 + row_idx*0.2, 0.2 +\
    \ col_idx*0.2])\n      return np.vstack([grid_centers, hole_center])\n\n  def _ensure_validity(c, r):\n      for _ in range(10):\n          v=0\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j]); rad_sum = r[i] + r[j]\n                  if dist < rad_sum: v+=1; scale = (dist/rad_sum)*(1.0-1e-9); r[i]*=scale; r[j]*=scale\n              if v==0: break\n      r_vec = r.reshape(-1, 1); c = np.clip(c, r_vec, 1.0 - r_vec)\n      return c, np.maximum(r, 1e-6)\n  \n  def cr_to_z(c, r): return np.concatenate([c.flatten(), r])\n  def z_to_cr(z): return z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), z[N*2:]\n  def objective_unpenalized(z): return -np.sum(z[N*2:])\n  def ineq_boundary(z):\n      c, r = z_to_cr(z); return np.concatenate([c[:,0]-r, 1-(c[:,0]+r), c[:,1]-r, 1-(c[:,1]+r)])\n  def ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n      c, r = z_to_cr(z); diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]; dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=-1))\n      iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1);\
    \ return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      np.random.seed(300) # Seed from my best experiment\n      \n      # --- Stage 1: Generate my best packing (abridged Voronoi Seeder) ---\n      # This is a simplified version of my best method to generate a high-quality, non-SOTA base\n      CANDIDATE_POOL_SIZE = 250; NUM_SEEDS_TO_REFINE = 20; PERTURBATION_MAG = 0.04\n      candidate_seeds = []\n      for i in range(CANDIDATE_POOL_SIZE):\n          grid_idx = np.random.randint(25); base_c = generate_grid_hole_seed(grid_idx)\n          perturbation = np.random.uniform(-PERTURBATION_MAG, PERTURBATION_MAG, size=base_c.shape)\n          candidate_seeds.append(np.clip(base_c + perturbation, 0, 1))\n\n      best_seed_score = -np.inf; base_centers, base_radii = (None, None)\n      bounds = [(0,1)]*N*2 + [(1e-6, 0.5)]*N\n      constraints = [{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap}]\n      # Just refine a few to get\
    \ a good base quickly\n      for seed_centers in candidate_seeds[:NUM_SEEDS_TO_REFINE]:\n          initial_z = cr_to_z(seed_centers, np.full(N, 0.05))\n          res = minimize(objective_unpenalized, initial_z, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 1000, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n          if res.success:\n              c, r = _ensure_validity(*z_to_cr(res.x)); score = np.sum(r)\n              if score > best_seed_score: best_seed_score = score; base_centers, base_radii = c, r\n      \n      if base_centers is None: return np.random.rand(N, 2), np.full(N, 0.05)\n\n      # --- Stage 2: Systematic Nudging on the generated packing ---\n      slacks = []\n      for i in range(N):\n          for j in range(i + 1, N):\n              dist = np.linalg.norm(base_centers[i] - base_centers[j])\n              slack = dist - (base_radii[i] + base_radii[j])\n              if slack > 1e-8: slacks.append({'pair': (i, j), 'slack': slack})\n      slacks.sort(key=lambda x: x['slack'])\n\
    \      nudge_targets = [s['pair'] for s in slacks[:5]]\n\n      def create_penalized_objective(encourage_pair):\n          def objective_penalized(z):\n              centers, radii = z_to_cr(z); base_obj = -np.sum(radii)\n              i, j = encourage_pair; dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n              penalty = np.maximum(0, dist - (radii[i] + radii[j] + 0.005))**2\n              return base_obj + 1e2 * penalty\n          return objective_penalized\n\n      overall_best_score = -np.inf; overall_best_packing = (None, None)\n      for target_pair in nudge_targets:\n          objective_fn = create_penalized_objective(target_pair)\n          initial_z = cr_to_z(base_centers, base_radii)\n          res = minimize(objective_fn, initial_z, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 500, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n          if res.success:\n              c, r = _ensure_validity(*z_to_cr(res.x)); score = np.sum(r)\n              if score > overall_best_score:\
    \ overall_best_score = score; overall_best_packing = (c, r)\n\n      if overall_best_packing[0] is None: return _ensure_validity(base_centers, base_radii)\n      return overall_best_packing\n```"
